@crew grieve-thea
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hello. Grieve, infirmary. If you're bleeding, it's Deck 3. If not, sit down anyway.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, {me}. Have you lost anything? Only, I've a box. Of found things.
- Hello. O positive. Sorry. That's yours. I say it instead of hello sometimes.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Oh. Hello, {me}. I'm glad it's you. You make the infirmary less quiet.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. I gave a glove back. Its owner had given up hope. So had I.
? mood:low
- Long shift. I worried all morning. Then I fixed it. Then I worried I hadn't.

== near
? act:work
- Corners tucked. Sheets straight. Every bed. It matters if you're the one in it.
? place:infirmary
- Sit there. Don't touch anything blue. That's a rule, I didn't make it.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I keep fish back home on New Aberdeen. My sister sends me how they're doing. All well.
? tier>=colleague
- I'm studying for my nursing exams. In the evenings. Mostly worrying, some studying.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- The lost-property box. One odd sock's been there for months. I live in hope.

== about
? bond:friends
- {friend} checks on me when I'm worrying. I worry less with {friend} about.

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Good morning. Did you sleep? Properly? Seven hours is the minimum. I'm just saying.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Hello. Long day. I've made every bed twice. Nobody's in them. That's good news.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Oh. You're back. I was going to check the records. In case. I didn't. I nearly did.

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Goodbye. Drink some water. That's what Nandakumar would say. So I'm saying it.
? tier>=friend
- Thank you. I worry less when I've talked to you. I don't know why that is.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Fine. All right. Nothing went wrong. Something might have. It didn't.

== near
? deck:2 time:night
- The stars are steady. I like that about them. They're always exactly where they were.
? act:meal
- I stay a while after meals. It's calmer. Nobody needs a bed changed in the mess.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- My fish back home are called One, Two and Three. My sister says they're doing well.
? tier>=friend
- I'm studying for my nursing exams. I'm very scared of them. Don't tell anyone.

== invite
? trad:observatory-night tier>=colleague
- Observatory night? It's very calm. Nobody bleeds. Would you come?

== accept
- Yes. All right. Yes. I'll be there. I'll be early.
== decline
- I can't. I'm sorry. Late shift. Can we do another day? A specific day?
== missed
- You didn't come. I hope nothing's wrong. Is anything wrong? Good.
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. I didn't tell anyone. Then I told you. That's fine.
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. Your blood type's a lucky one. That's not a real thing. Happy birthday.   #funny
== hint
- Could we talk? Somewhere quiet. Not the infirmary.
